    fullDescription: "Vosoritide (BMN111; Voxzogo) is a synthetic C-type natriuretic peptide (CNP) analog developed by BioMarin Pharmaceuticals for treatment of achondroplasia, the most common form of skeletal dysplasia. Native CNP is produced by endochondral ossification growth plate chondrocytes that acts on NPR-B (guanylyl cyclase-B/GUCY2B) in an autocrine/paracrine manner to promote chondrocyte proliferation, matrix secretion, and longitudinal bone growth — counteracting FGFR3-mediated MAPK signaling that suppresses chondrocyte proliferation. In achondroplasia, gain-of-function FGFR3 mutations constitutively activate ERK1/2 and STAT signaling, accelerating chondrocyte differentiation and reducing proliferative zone expansion, resulting in disproportionate short stature. CNP-NPR-B-cGMP signaling suppresses ERK1/2 downstream of FGFR3 through a PDE2-mediated cross-talk mechanism, providing the molecular rationale for vosoritide's therapeutic approach.\n\nVosoritide incorporates a Pro-Arg N-terminal extension relative to native CNP(1-38) that confers resistance to aminopeptidase N degradation, extending plasma half-life for once-daily SC dosing. In growth plate chondrocyte cultures from FGFR3 gain-of-function mouse models, vosoritide at nanomolar concentrations activates NPR-B-cGMP signaling and restores chondrocyte proliferative zone height toward normal. In Fgfr3 Y367C/+ achondroplasia mouse models, once-daily vosoritide SC administration significantly increases femur, tibia, and lumbar vertebral body length compared to vehicle-treated littermates, with improved proportionality of skeletal dimensions demonstrating systemic growth plate correction.\n\nVosoritide (Voxzogo) received FDA approval in 2021 for achondroplasia in pediatric patients 5 years and older whose growth plates have not closed, based on Phase III data demonstrating statistically significant improvements in annualized growth velocity (mean +1.57 cm/year versus placebo). Research applications include studying NPR-B receptor biology in bone development, investigating cGMP-PDE2-ERK cross-talk coordinating FGFR3 and natriuretic peptide signaling in growth plate chondrocytes, and developing CNP analogs for other skeletal dysplasias caused by constitutively active tyrosine kinase receptors. Its established NPR-B pharmacology also makes vosoritide a research tool for studying CNP roles in cardiovascular tissue and the nervous system (NPR-B in dorsal root ganglia contributing to axon growth).",
